<h1>Hai Ba Trung by Motorbike: Motorbike Rental Planning in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Hai Ba Trung is the district that sits between the postcard and the river. South and east of Hoan Kiem, it holds the French-quarter boulevards and their cafes, the shopping streets, the park layer, and the long river dike that runs down its eastern side, and all of it rides. Basing a motorbike stay here puts the Old Quarter minutes away and the dike road under the wheels, which is one of the city's great riding habits. The fact that shapes every plan is the counter's location: Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu operates from 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, and the rental starts and ends there. This page plans the whole rental around that, with no invented branches, no delivery promises and no quoted journey times.</p>
<p>We cover where the district sits in a rider's plan, the pickup question answered straight, riding Hai Ba Trung's own streets, choosing a rental period, grouping the stay's days, matching the machine to the plan, handling extensions and returns, and a checklist to run before you commit. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and browse wider riding advice in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>.</p>
